    {
      q: 'How long should a hot water system last?',
      a: 'Electric storage systems typically last 8–12 years. Gas continuous flow units last 10–15+ years with regular servicing. Heat pump systems have a similar lifespan to electric storage. If your system is over 10 years old and failing repeatedly, replacement is usually more cost-effective than ongoing repairs.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What are the signs my hot water system needs replacing?',
      a: 'Signs include no hot water, water that takes too long to heat, rust-coloured water, a leaking tank (usually a failed sacrificial anode or a cracked vessel), unusual popping or rumbling noises, and repeated component failures.',
